From e0edfdba1afdcec30a5ab899bc665c3b33f5f4eb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mira <mira@example.invalid>
Date: Thu, 28 May 2026 23:44:04 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] [feature](be) Add SrunwindProcMaps cache for
 snapshot-remote-unwind native stack collector

Mirrors OceanBase's ObProcMaps shape (Phase C ob_proc_maps) so the
coordinator can resolve PCs to DSO offsets after the worker handler
captures a register+stack snapshot. Duplicated rather than shared with
Phase C: the four phase2 variants are isolation experiments and the
shared infrastructure refactor is out of scope.

Adds load_thread_stack_bounds() (per-tid /proc/self/task/<tid>/maps
parse) so the handler's 8 KiB stack memcpy can be clamped to the
[stack] VMA before the read. Keeps MemoryMap.readable on the row so the
coordinator can also validate non-stack memory ranges when reading
return addresses out of the snapshot.

Reference: <ob>/deps/oblib/src/lib/signal/ob_signal_struct.h:87-107
Reference: <ob>/deps/oblib/src/lib/signal/ob_signal_struct.cpp:52-88
